Atmanatmashrayah purvam mayaya sasrije gunan. The one who is in the form of a wave, the true resolve, the creator, the lord of the waves. 12. Meaning of the word

Atmana—by one's own personal power; Atma—of the soul; Aashrayah—refuge; Purvam—first; Mayaya—by one's creative power;
Sasruje—created; Gunan—the fundamental qualities of nature; Taah—through them; Idam—this (universe); Satya—in the form of truth;
Ejatmam—desires; Srujasi—create; Attsi—destroy; Avasi—preserve;
Ishwarah—the controller. You are the shelter of all beings, and because of being omnipresent, with your willpower,
you fulfill all your desires. With your personal creative power, you initially revealed the primal qualities of nature,
and through them, you create, sustain, and destroy this universe. You are the destroyer of the demons, the earth, the elements, and the enemies.
For the incarnation of destruction, for the protection of the saints. 13. Meaning of the word

Sah—He; Tvam—You; Bhoo-dhar—As kings; Bhoothanam—Appearing; Daitya-pramatha-raksasam—Of various
types of demons; Avatirnah—You have descended; Vinashaya—For destruction; Sadhunam—Of saintly men; Rakshanaya—For protection
of; Cha—And also..

You are the destroyer, who has descended on this earth to destroy the demons, gods, and evil spirits who consider themselves kings,
and to protect the saints. Dishtya te nihata daityo leelayayam hayaakritih. Whose laughter is a thunderbolt, they do not believe the night. 14. Meaning of the word

Drishtya—(by our) good fortune; Te—by you; Nihatha—killed; Daityah—demons; Lilaya—in play; Ayam—this;
Hay-Aakritih—of the shape of a horse; Yasya—whose; Heshita—with a mocking laugh; Santrastah—frightened; Tyajanti—leave;
are; Animishah—the gods; Divam—heaven;
This demon with the shape of a horse was creating so much terror that from his screaming
the gods, being frightened, had left their kingdom of heaven. But fortunately for us,
you killed him in the game itself. Chanuram Mushtikam chaiva mallanayamshcha hastinam. I see the slain in the evening, O Lord. 15.
